  "description": "Visual tree/field editor for CrudApi's AI-generated tenant config JSON — a viewer/editor over the pipeline CrudConfigApplicationService already produces, not a reimplementation of it. Reads/writes through the same git-backed store (WebSvc.GitOps), with version history read from real commits rather than a shadow database table. No SQL storage of its own — sessions persist to a JSON file, same pattern as WebSvc.SqliteAdmin. Platform-admin only, reached via a signed one-click handoff from CrudAdmin's Databases page. v1.0.1 fixes a real bug found in production: an unset GitHub token read as CrudApi's \"(not-configured)\" placeholder string, not null, so the readiness check was fooled into treating \"not configured\" as \"not found\" — now correctly distinguishes not-configured / not-found / a genuine GitOps error, each with a clear message instead of a raw exception.",
